{title: The church triumphant}
{subtitle: Hymnal 231}

{comment: Chorus}
I’m talking about the church in the book of Revelation
It’s built on the rock, It’s got a firm foundation
It’s been thru the flood and it’s been thru the fire
One of these days the church is gonna move up higher
It’s the church, triumphant O Lord
And it’s built by the hand of the Lord

{comment: Verse 1}
It’s the old ship of Zion, It’s hope for the lost and dying
It’s a soul saving station, The tower of salvation
It’s the church, triumphant O Lord
And it’s built by the hand of the Lord
It’s been thru the storm, but the wind couldn’t turn it
It’s been in the fire, but the fire couldn’t burn it
Fed to the lions, but the lions couldn’t eat it
Fought a lot of wars, but never defeated
It’s the church, triumphant O lord
And it’s built by the hand of Lord
